 ----
 
 This can help in CI environments to prevent misconfiguration:
 For example, a CI build should probably never create a new the violation store, but operate on
 an existing one.
 
+With `freeze.store.default.integrity=repair`, each initialization checks the current index and files on disk,
+even if the store was initialized before. Entries are broken if their paths are invalid or do not refer to
+regular files directly within the store folder; repair removes these entries without deleting their paths.
+Entries whose files are empty or contain only line breaks are resolved; repair removes both the entries and
+their files. For a resolved symbolic link, its target file is deleted as well.
+
+Entries sharing the same file name or referring to the same file (including through symbolic or hard links,
+even outside the folder) are always left untouched during initialization, even if otherwise broken or resolved.
+Unreferenced files are also left untouched. In repair mode, saving no violations forgets a known rule and
+deletes its file unless another entry shares it; unknown rules without violations are not saved.
+If deleting a forgotten rule's file fails, saving fails and its entry is retained.
+
 As mentioned in <<Overriding configuration>>, these properties can be passed as system properties as needed.
